END-USER LICENSE AGREEMENT (EULA) FOR VIM DOJO

Last Updated: September 24, 2026

Please read this End-User License Agreement ("Agreement") carefully before
downloading, installing, or using the Vim Dojo application ("Software"). By
using the Software, you agree to be bound by the terms of this Agreement. If
you do not agree, do not install or use the Software.

This Agreement is between you and Michael Bergen
("the developer"). Questions and support: webtechmike@gmail.com.


1. License Grant & Paid Upgrades

   Free Tier License: Vim Dojo grants you a limited, non-exclusive,
   non-transferable, revocable license to use the Software's first three belts
   (White, Yellow and Orange) for personal evaluation.

   Premium Level License: Access to content beyond the first three belts,
   including the daily kata past Black Belt, requires the purchase of a
   premium software license fee. Upon verified payment, your license expands
   to unlock the full training curriculum for personal use on one device at
   a time. To move your license to another device, run "vim-dojo --deactivate"
   on the old device first.

   Scope: This license is strictly for personal, non-commercial educational
   use.

   Open Source Components: This Software may utilize components governed by
   open-source licenses. Nothing in this Agreement replaces or overrides your
   rights under those specific open-source licenses. These components and
   their licenses are listed in the THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES file included with
   the Software.


2. Restrictions on Use

   You agree not to, and will not permit others to:

   Bypass Licensing: Modify, hack, or attempt to bypass the software checks
   that restrict access to content beyond the first three belts without a
   valid paid upgrade.

   Reverse Engineer: Decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer, or attempt to
   derive the source code of the Software.

   Redistribute: Rent, lease, lend, sell, redistribute, or sublicense the
   Software, its level configurations, or any interactive training assets.


3. Local Data & Privacy

   Local Storage: Your training progress, metrics, and scores are stored only
   on your device. Vim Dojo does not sync them online.

   License Verification: To verify a premium license, the Software contacts
   our payment provider, Polar, when you activate or deactivate a license key
   and about once a week afterwards. It sends your license key, a one-way
   hash of your device's hardware identifier, and your computer's name.
   Nothing else is sent.

   Data Loss: Because there is no cloud synchronization, backing up your app
   data is your responsibility. The developer is not responsible for lost
   progress resulting from app deletion, device failure, or factory resets.


4. Intellectual Property Rights

   Ownership: The developer retains all right, title, and interest in and to
   the Software. This includes all code, interface designs, training
   curricula, keyboard challenge logic, graphics, and text. This Agreement
   grants a license to use the Software; it does not sell the underlying
   intellectual property.


5. Limitation of Liability

   "As-Is" Provision: The Software is provided "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" with
   all faults and defects without warranty of any kind.

   Muscle Memory & Keyboard Habituation: Vim Dojo is a training utility. The
   developer is not liable for any productivity loss, accidental command line
   errors, file deletions, or altered muscle memory resulting from your
   practice or your customized keyboard layouts.

   Maximum Liability: To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the
   developer's total liability for any claims arising out of this Agreement
   shall be limited to the amount you actually paid to unlock the Software.


6. Governing Law & Global Distribution

   Governing Law: This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in
